 <sys:String x:Key="L.Faq.Title">FAQ</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Faq.Subtitle">Answers to common questions about GivreClone.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Faq.Q1">What is GivreClone for?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Faq.A1">It turns each network interface (Ethernet, Wi-Fi, 4G hotspot…) into a local proxy. Each proxy sends traffic out through its interface's IP.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Faq.Q2">How do I use it with GivreLauncher?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Faq.A2">Enable an adapter, copy its URL, then paste it as an account's proxy in GivreLauncher.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Faq.Q3">Does the port change on every activation?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Faq.A3">By default yes (automatic port). Set a fixed port in the adapter settings to keep the same URL.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Faq.Q4">Is it safe?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Faq.A4">The proxy is local, on your machine. It only relays your own traffic and sends nothing elsewhere.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Faq.Q5">Are the logs sensitive?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Faq.A5">They show the destinations of the traffic passing through. Avoid sharing them as-is.</sys:String>

