 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.TabPlanning">Schedule</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.Enable">Schedule on</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.AutoConnect">Auto connect</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.AutoConnectTip">Connects the account at the start of each slot (straight into the game) and disconnects it outside the slots, once the current fight is over — even if launched manually — after a countdown you can cancel. With no slot defined, nothing is ever disconnected.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.AutoConnectHint">Auto connect: the account logs into its LAST PLAYED CHARACTER — play this character once on this account. Outside the slots, an account in game on this character is disconnected after a 10 s countdown you can cancel (it then stays online until its next slot). A manual stop during a slot is not relaunched before the slot ends. Scripts added from a file are reloaded at the start of each slot.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.Hint">The script auto-starts during the ranges below and stops outside them. Humanization slightly shifts the times so it never starts exactly on the hour.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.Jitter">Humanize (± min)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.CaptureScript">Freeze current script</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.CaptureHint">Saves the Lua editor script as the one the schedule will run.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.CaptureTemplate">The Lua editor only shows the sample script: nothing was frozen. Write or load your script first.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.Library">Script library</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.LibraryHint">Your scripts: load a.lua or freeze the editor, then assign a specific script to each range below.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.SlotScript">Range script</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.SlotScriptHint">Script run during this range (picked from the library above). "✕" removes the assignment: the range then runs the frozen fallback script.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.SlotDefaultN">Range {0}</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.Conflict">This range overlaps another one — adjust the days or times.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.ScriptMissing">Script not found in the library:</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.ScriptMissingTip">This script was deleted from the library: the range runs nothing until you pick another one in the list, add a script with this name again, or remove the assignment ("Remove": the range then runs the frozen fallback script).</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.ClearScript">Remove</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.ClearScriptTip">Removes the script from this range: it will run the frozen fallback script ("Freeze current script"), or nothing if there is none.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.ScriptRelinked">Schedule: range "{0}" → script "{1}" (assignment restored).</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.ScriptRenameTip">Press Enter or click elsewhere to confirm the name, Esc to cancel. Ranges using this script follow the rename.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.ScriptName">Script name</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Planning.ScriptDefault">Script {0}</sys:String>
