 <!-- Bots: Combat tab (i18n) -->
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.AutoPlay">Automatically play my combat turns</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.AutoSpells">Automatic mode: all my learned spells</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.AutoSpellsTip">Plays with every learned spell that deals damage, on top of your list, ordered by damage per AP. A spell in your list keeps its settings; unchecked, it is left out.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PreFight">Auto pre-fight: position and get ready</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Placement">Placement</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Placement.Legacy">By style</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Placement.None">None</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Placement.Near">Near</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Placement.Far">Far</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlacementHint">None: keep your cell. Near / Far: minimize / maximize the distance to the nearest enemy, independently of style. By style preserves existing profiles' behavior.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Challenge">Pick and validate a challenge every fight</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.AutoRevive">Auto-revive (Phoenix)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeHint">Among the accepted challenges, GivreClone takes the one that pays the most on average (success chance × bonus).</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.SectionChallenges">Challenges</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeNeedsPreFight">Turn on &quot;Auto pre-fight&quot; above: the challenge is picked during placement.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeRules">Adapt the AI to active challenges</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeRulesHint">Statue: doesn't move · Versatile: each spell once per turn · First, Elitist, Focus…: a single target · Bold, Careful, Sticky…: forced end-of-turn cell. Also applies to a challenge picked by hand.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeBonus">Bonus</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.BonusXp">XP</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.BonusLoot">Loot</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeBonusHint">GivreClone announces this bonus to the server every fight (Socket and classic modes); the journal shows the bonus confirmed by the server.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeList">Accepted challenges ({0}/{1})…</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeListTitle">Accepted challenges</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeListSub">Untick the challenges GivreClone must never pick. Failing a challenge costs nothing: only the bonus is lost.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeSupportEnforced">AI adapted</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeSupportEnforcedTip">The AI changes how it plays to keep this challenge.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeSupportNatural">No action</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeSupportNaturalTip">Nothing special to do: it passes or not depending on the fight.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeSupportNone">Not handled</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeSupportNoneTip">The AI can't keep this challenge (weapon, indirect damage, team coordination…).</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeDefaults">Recommended</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ChallengeFallback">Challenge #{0}</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Style">AI style</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Target">Target</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Speed">Speed</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.SpellsByPriority">Spells cast by priority</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.AddSpell">＋ Add a spell…</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ColSpell">Spell</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ColPriority">Priority</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PriorityTip">Cast order: the SMALLER the number (and the HIGHER in the list), the higher the priority. Drag this badge — or use the arrows — to reorder.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ColPerTurn">× / turn</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ColPerTarget">× / target</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PerTargetCfgTip">Max casts of this spell on the same target per turn (0 = game limit only).</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ColCooldown">Cooldown</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CooldownTip">Cooldown: minimum turns between two casts (0 = none)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ColSelf">Self</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ToggleTip">Enable / disable</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.SelfCastTip">Cast on myself (buff/heal)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ColBuff">Buff</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.SelfBuffTip">Buff: cast on myself even with no enemy in range. Unchecked = offensive area spell, cast only if an enemy is inside the area.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Conditions">Conditions</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondTip">The spell is cast only if ALL its conditions are met. 0 (or 0–100 for HP) = disabled. Target/self HP in %.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondTgtHp">Target HP %</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondSelfHp">Self HP %</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondMinAp">Min AP</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondMinTurn">Turn ≥</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondMinEnemies">Enemies ≥</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondMinAoeHits">In zone ≥</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondGroupTarget">Target HP</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondGroupSelf">Self HP</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondGroupContext">Context</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondHpHint">0–100% = any target</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondSelfHint">0–100% = always</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondActive">Active conditions</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondTgtHpTip">Only cast the spell if the TARGET's HP (%) is within the min–max range. E.g. 0–30 = finish a weak enemy; 20–100 = skip near-dead targets.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondTgtHpDesc">Target HP % range (0–100 = any target).</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondSelfHpTip">Only cast the spell if YOUR HP (%) is within the min–max range. E.g. 0–50 = heal/defensive when low.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondSelfHpDesc">Your HP % range (0–100 = always).</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondHpMinTip">Minimum HP % of the range.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondHpMaxTip">Maximum HP % of the range.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondMinApTip">Minimum AP: only cast this spell if you have at least this many AP when casting (0 = no condition).</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondMinTurnTip">From turn: only cast this spell from this turn number onward (1 = from turn 1; 0 = no condition). E.g. 3 = wait until turn 3.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondMinEnemiesTip">Minimum enemies: only cast this spell if at least this many enemies are alive (0 = no condition). E.g. 2 = for an area spell.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.CondMinAoeHitsTip">Minimum enemies in zone (AREA spells only): only cast this spell if the BEST target cell catches at least this many enemies in its zone (0 = no condition). Avoids wasting a wide AoE on a single target.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.RemoveTip">Remove the spell</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ColOrder">Order</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.NoSpells">No spell in the rotation — add some via the dropdown above.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.MoveUpTip">Move up (higher priority)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.MoveDownTip">Move down (lower priority)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.MaxCasts">Max casts / turn</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.TabBehavior">Behavior</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.TabSpells">Spells</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.TabTeam">Team</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.SpellConfigTitle">SPELL CONFIGURATION</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.TabEssential">Essential</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.TabPlacement">Placement &amp; zones</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.TabAdvConditions">Advanced conditions</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.QuickRules">Quick rules</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.RuleEnabled">Spell enabled</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.RuleOnMe">Cast directly on me</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.RuleBuff">Buff: cast even with no enemy in range</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.RuleSummon">Summon (place on a free cell)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.SummonTip">The spell summons a creature on a free walkable cell in range instead of targeting an enemy. Give it a low priority (small number) to summon early in the turn.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.RuleTargetAlly">Target an ally (heal/buff)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.TargetAllyTip">The spell targets a TEAMMATE (or your own summon) instead of an enemy: it aims at the lowest-HP ally castable from here. Combine with the target HP window (e.g. "only heal below 60%"). Self-cast is still handled by "Cast on me".</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.MaxSummons">Max summons</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlaceRange">Cast range</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlaceRangeTip">Bounds the distance at which the bot casts this spell. 0 = the spell's natural range (range boosts included).</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlaceRangeMin">Min distance</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlaceRangeMinTip">Don't cast closer than this: the bot positions farther away (per-spell kite). 0 = no minimum.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlaceRangeMax">Max range</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlaceRangeMaxTip">Caps the cast range: the bot closes in instead of sniping from afar. 0 = natural max range.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlaceRangeHint">0 = automatic. Min distance = keep your distance (kite); max range = force closing in.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlaceMove">Movement</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.NeverApproach">Never approach (all spells and end of turn)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.NeverApproachHint">Blocks casting reposition and any move closer to the nearest enemy, including challenges. Retreat and lateral movement remain allowed. An incompatible challenge may fail; initial placement stays independent.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlaceApproach">Move to cast this spell</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlaceApproachTip">On: the bot finds a cast cell and moves to it. Off: it only casts this spell when ALREADY in range.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlaceApproachHint">Uncheck to cast only this spell in place. End-of-turn approach is still allowed: use Never approach under Behavior to block it for all spells and the end of turn.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.PlaceActive">Custom placement</sys:String>
 <!-- Combat turn simulator -->
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Simulate">Simulate a turn</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Title">Turn simulator</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Hint">Place your character and enemies, set AP/MP/range, then run: the bot replays its rotation step by step.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.ModeEnemy">Place an enemy</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.ModeMe">Place me</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.ModeErase">Erase</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Budget">Turn budget</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Ap">AP</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Mp">MP</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Range">Range</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Turn">Turn no.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Run">Simulate</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Reset">Reset</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Play">Play</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Pause">Pause</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.StepBack">Previous step</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.StepFwd">Next step</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Journal">Turn log</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Hud">Turn {0} · AP {1} · MP {2} · {3} enemy(ies)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Summary">{0} cast(s) · {1} move(s) · {2} KO</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.LogMove">Move → cell {0}</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.LogCast">{0} → enemy (distance {1})</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.LogCastSelf">{0} on self</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.LogPass">Passes the turn (nothing castable)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.LogNoEnemy">No enemy on the board</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.LogEnd">End of turn</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.EnemyHp">Enemy HP</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.MultiTurn">Replay until the fight ends</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.MaxTurns">Max turns</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.LogCastDmg">{0} → enemy (-{1} HP, distance {2})</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.LogKill">{0} → enemy defeated ({1} left)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.LogTurnSep">— Turn {0} —</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.SummaryCleared">Pack cleared in {0} turn(s) · {1} KO</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Sim.Disclaimer">Average damage, no resistances/retaliation — a comprehension tool, not an exact replay.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Done">Done</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.Configure">Configure</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.TagEnemy">Enemy</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.TagSelf">Self</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.TagBuff">Buff</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.ConfigureTip">Configure this spell: essential, placement &amp; zones, advanced conditions.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.TeamSoon">Group / multi-account — soon</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Combat.TeamSoonHint">Group management (leader / followers, invites, inter-bot wait, Lua controller) is coming in a dedicated batch.</sys:String>
 <!-- Team (multi-account) -->
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.NeedTwo">Launch at least 2 accounts in game to compose a team.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.Compose">Compose the team</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.Leader">Team leader</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.PickLeader">Pick the leader…</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.Follow">Follow</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.RoleLeader">Leader</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.RoleFollower">Team member</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.Form">Form the group</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.Disband">Disband the team</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.FollowSection">Follow</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.SyncDelay">Random inter-bot delay (min → max, ms)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.FollowToggle">Auto-follow the leader</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.CombatToggle">Join the leader's fights</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.FollowHelp">Followers stick to the leader (cell + map, even off world-graph) and wait for him before changing area.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.CombatHelp">Followers join every fight; the leader waits for them before engaging AND before picking the challenge.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.Registered">Registered members (online or not)</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.FollowerLocked">This account is driven by its team (the leader is in charge): script and planning are locked. Only the Combat tab stays editable.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="L.Bots.Team.FollowHint">Once the party is formed, followers automatically join the leader's map (staggered by the delay). Leader in a fight: they wait. A follower running its own script keeps control.</sys:String>
